# OpenAPI and DTO Rules

- The OpenAPI specification under `/docs/openapi/openapi.yaml` is the HTTP contract.
- DTOs MUST represent explicit input/output contracts and MUST NOT be Eloquent models.
- Financial values MUST use decimal-safe representations.
- DTOs MUST NOT accept fields that the authenticated actor is not allowed to change.
- Any endpoint added to Laravel MUST be documented in OpenAPI before implementation is considered complete.
- Breaking HTTP changes require a documented versioning decision.
- Controllers MUST map HTTP input to DTOs/use cases and MUST NOT contain domain rules.
